Hi — following the review comments on this PR (the maintainer bot noting tables "can become wider **without gaining a horizontal scroll container**", and Greptile noting right-hand columns are unreachable on narrow viewports): I have a working complement to offer.

## The missing half: a horizontal scroll wrapper for transcript tables

On mobile/narrow viewports, `.msg-body`'s `overflow-wrap:anywhere` crushes table columns to ~1 character, and even with widened content width the table has no horizontal scroll escape. The fix I've been running locally (and verified in daily mobile use):

**`static/messages.js`** — `enhanceMarkdownTables()` wraps each table in a scroll container (idempotent, skips `.csv-table-wrap`):

```js
const tableParent=table.parentElement;
let scrollWrap=null;
if(tableParent&&!tableParent.classList.contains('markdown-table-scroll')){
  scrollWrap=document.createElement('div');
  scrollWrap.className='markdown-table-scroll';
  tableParent.insertBefore(scrollWrap, table);
  scrollWrap.appendChild(table);
}
```

**`static/style.css`** — the wrapper + word-boundary wrap (undoes the chat body's letter-crush for cells):

```css
.markdown-table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;margin:8px 0;max-width:100%;}
.markdown-table-scroll>table{width:auto;min-width:100%;margin:0;}
.markdown-table-scroll th,.markdown-table-scroll td{overflow-wrap:normal;word-break:normal;}
```

Behavior: the table fills the container (`min-width:100%`), wraps at word boundaries, and **only** overflows (wrapper scrolls) when a column's widest unbreakable token can't fit — no more letter-crushed columns, no unreachable right-hand columns. The filter box stays pinned above the scroll area. Same pattern as the existing `.csv-table-wrap`.

