## Summary

I read the complete two-file diff, the full modified regression file and its `origin/master` version, plus the surrounding `autoResize()` implementation at `static/messages.js:6733-6782`. This is a conservative optimization: it skips only growth whose already-laid-out `scrollHeight` fits inside the current `offsetHeight`. Deletes, equal-length replacements, wrapped-line growth, and any stale tracker state fall through to the existing measurement path. I do not see a blocker.

## Code reference

The new gate at `static/messages.js:6736-6753` is narrow:

```javascript
const _nextValueLength=String(el.value||"").length;
const _isGrowing=_nextValueLength>_composerLastResizeValueLength;
const _fitsCurrentHeight=el.scrollHeight<=el.offsetHeight;
if(_isGrowing&&_fitsCurrentHeight){
  _composerLastResizeValueLength=_nextValueLength;
  return;
}
```

That ordering matters. The browser has already recalculated textarea layout for the new value before `autoResize()` reads `scrollHeight`, so a newline or newly wrapped line that needs more height cannot take the shortcut. The full path at `static/messages.js:6754-6780` still snapshots transcript scroll position, performs the `auto` to measured-height round trip, restores `scrollTop`, updates the tracked length, and invokes the genuine-growth repin guard.

