## Diagnosis / recommendation

The module-level length tracker is safe under session and draft replacement. A stale high value causes an unnecessary full resize, not an incorrect skip. A stale low value can skip only if the replacement already fits the current height, which is exactly the no-op case. Equal-length replacements also take the full path, which is useful for IME and text substitutions where line wrapping can change without a length change.

